    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0124" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d45-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-16">October 16, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. 459. Prime Minister to President Roosevelt</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <list>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>I entirely agree with the telegram you have sent to Uncle Joe about <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Eureka</hi>. Let me know what he
                        replies.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>Please also see Saint Mark 9 verses 5 and 6 especially sixth verse.<anchor
                            n="2" xml:id="d45-f2"/>
                    </item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d45-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d45-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently sent via military channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d45-f2" n="2" xml:id="d45-f2-content">
                <p>The following footnote was typed on the source text by the White House Map
                    Room:</p>
                <p>“Saint Mark 9</p>
                <list>
                    <item>“5. And Peter answered and said to
                        Jesus, Master, it is good for us to be here: and let us make three
                        tabernacles; one for thee, and one for Moses, and one for Elias.</item>
                    <item>“6. For he wist not what to say; for they were sore afraid.”</item>
                </list>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
